   in WidgetChrome/AlertCountWidget. project.yml does NOT set
   SWIFT_TREAT_WARNINGS_AS_ERRORS, so it is a warning the real `xcodebuild build
   test` gate would not fail on. Left unchanged: a string-interpolation rewrite
   would entangle the .xcstrings key-based localization of live-updating relative
   dates, and it is out of this prompt's scope.)

--- genuine bug found via the real SDK and FIXED (committed 4b5dc7c0) ---
  WidgetPreviews.swift applied `.environment(\.widgetFamily, .systemMedium)` to
  three plain-view #Previews. `EnvironmentValues.widgetFamily` is GET-ONLY, so the
  key path is a `KeyPath`, not a `WritableKeyPath`, and `.environment(_:_:)` does
  not type-check on it — a hard compile error the deferred gate WOULD have hit:
    error: cannot convert value of type 'KeyPath<EnvironmentValues, WidgetFamily>'
           to expected argument type 'WritableKeyPath<EnvironmentValues, V>'
  `.previewContext(WidgetPreviewContext(family:))` is also rejected — the #Preview
  macro ignores previewContext. Correct minimal fix: remove the three invalid
  modifiers (widgetFamily defaults to .systemMedium, preserving the intent) and
  keep the writable `.environment(\.colorScheme,.dark)` /
  `(\.dynamicTypeSize,.accessibility3)`. Swept the app: no other `\.widgetFamily`
  injections exist. After the fix, swiftlint/swiftformat/placeholder stay green and
  the full surface compiles clean (above). This bug was invisible to the
  predecessor, which excluded WidgetPreviews.swift from its CLT-only typecheck.

  CONCLUSION: the BLOCKED determination was a pre-Xcode artifact. With real Xcode
  the runnable verification is STRONGER than every accepted predecessor's, a real
  defect was caught + fixed, and the only residual is the same full-app
  build/test deferral the convention already records. Corrected to
  EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE. Git history retains the original BLOCKED log at b545d750.

